{"name":"Zuni","hex":"#008996","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Zuni","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the Zuni people or their traditional language."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of a Native American Pueblo people, native to the Zuni River valley."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Zuni"}],"entries":[{"title":"Zuni people","blocks":[{"text":"The Zuni are Native American Pueblo peoples native to the Zuni River valley. The Zuni people today are federally recognized as the Zuni Tribe of the Zuni Reservation, New Mexico, and most live in the Pueblo of Zuni on the Zuni River, a tributary of the Little Colorado River, in western New Mexico, United States. The Pueblo of Zuni is 55 km (34 mi) south of Gallup, New Mexico. Traditional Zuni homes in the Pueblo are multi level adobe houses. In addition to the reservation, the tribe owns trust lands in Catron County, New Mexico, and Apache County, Arizona. The Zuni call their homeland Halona Idiwan’a or Middle Place. The word Zuni is believed to derive from the Western Keres language (Acoma) word sɨ̂‧ni, or a cognate thereof."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Zuni_map.svg/330px-Zuni_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zuni_people"},{"title":"Zuni language","blocks":[{"text":"Zuni is a language of the Zuni people, indigenous to western New Mexico and eastern Arizona in the southwestern United States. It is spoken by around 9,500 people, especially in the vicinity of Zuni Pueblo, New Mexico, and, much less commonly, in parts of Arizona."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Zuni_lang.png/330px-Zuni_lang.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zuni_language"},{"title":"Zuni (rocket)","blocks":[{"text":"The Zuni 5-inch Folding-Fin Aircraft Rocket (FFAR), or simply Zuni, is a 5.0 in (127 mm) unguided rocket developed by the Hunter Douglas Division of Bridgeport Brass Company and deployed by the United States Armed Forces, and the French Air Force. The rocket was developed for both air-to-air and air-to-ground operations. It can be used to carry various types of warheads, including chaff for countermeasures. It is usually fired from the LAU-10 rocket pod, holding four rockets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Zuni_unguided_rocket.jpg/330px-Zuni_unguided_rocket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zuni_(rocket)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Zuni-girl-with-jar2.png/500px-Zuni-girl-with-jar2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Zuni-girl-with-jar2.png/500px-Zuni-girl-with-jar2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZuni-girl-with-jar2.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Zuni_Salt_Lake.jpg/500px-Zuni_Salt_Lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Zuni_Salt_Lake.jpg/1280px-Zuni_Salt_Lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Zuni_Salt_Lake.jpg/500px-Zuni_Salt_Lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Zuni Salt Lake, New Mexico, where the Zuni have harvested salt for centuries","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZuni_Salt_Lake.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/We-Wa%2C_a_Zuni_berdache%2C_weaving_-_NARA_-_523796_%28cropped